# Benchmark correctness gate.
#
# Builds every bench/ kernel both ways (baseline llc, and nybbler + the same
# llc) and asserts the two produce byte-identical output. This catches a
# benchmark kernel drifting out of correctness -- a fast kernel computing the
# wrong thing is not a result.
#
# Timing is deliberately *not* asserted here. CI runners are shared and noisy,
# so a speedup threshold would flake; the numbers are produced by running
# `bash bench/run.sh` on a quiet machine (see docs/benchmarks.md).
#
# The quoting on PLUGIN matters: the repo path may contain spaces.
#
# RUN: env OPT="%opt" LLC="%llc" CLANG="%clang" PLUGIN="%nybbler" \
# RUN:     bash "%bench_dir/run.sh" --check-only | %FileCheck "%s"

# CHECK: CHECKSUM MATCH arith_i4
# CHECK: CHECKSUM MATCH cmp_i4
# CHECK: CHECKSUM MATCH field_i2
# CHECK: CHECKSUM MATCH mask_i1
# CHECK-NOT: CHECKSUM MISMATCH
